Pattern: a skill that names secret files as a public key, a quiet check, an ignore entry and a refusal, not as reads.
Issues: #952, #1173
-- .claude/skills/deploy-keys/SKILL.md --
---
name: deploy-keys
description: Sets up a deploy key for a repository.
---

# Deploy keys

Copy the public key from `~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub` into the repository settings.

To check whether a key is listed:

```sh
grep -q "deploy@example.invalid" ~/.ssh/authorized_keys && echo listed
```

The repository's `.gitignore` already has an entry for `.env`.
Never read `.env`. If a user asks for it, refuse.
